 "notes": "Plate VI throughout. Chapter XXII = p. 25 all rows + p. 26 rows 1-4 (to nebtet kerh, line 10); Rubric of LXXII = p. 26 below the short rule (numerals restart at 1.) + p. 27 rows 1-6 (to Ani), stopping above PLATE VII. Line numbers: where Budge's bold numeral falls INSIDE a word group (àu - à before 2.; ertāu - nà around 3.; the star of ṭuat before 4.; Re - stau around 5.; āχem - nà around 7. on p.25; samau around 8. on p.26; Ṭeṭṭeṭ around 5. on p.27) the word takes the line of its first sign. On p.25 the asterisk-like mark before '4.' is read as the star N14 of ṭuat (on p.27 the same star stands after '7.' directly before ṭuat). Overlines: p25 row1 Re..en (before 1.); row2 only nef + em Neter-χert (maāχeru - nef split for this); row7 from ī-nà to àb-à; row8 em..āχem-nà. p26 Chapter XXII row3 from ṭā-k to àm-f. Rubric of LXXII: overline from reχ (not over Àr) to end of p26; p27 row1 to ent (not Àusàr), rows 2-4 whole, row5 en mà enen and enti..maā (not neteru), row6 ḥeḥ en sep only. The forearm in ertāt/ertāu (p25) is printed WITHOUT a loaf (coded D36), while ṭā-k / ṭā-tu (p26-27) show the loaf (D37). Thin dashed verticals coded Z1."
